      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "While I am a Quest player, I can’t blame PC players for not choosing a cross platform avatar. If they are used to play with a set of avatars and those are not compatible with Quest, forcing them to use cross platform avatars feels wrong imho. It’s like having to wear clothes you really don’t like.\n\nI believe this is not a players’ problem, but a creators’ problem. It’s up to them to support Quest and the community, and create avatars that work nicely on both platforms. Unfortunately I believe a part of them is just not doing this, or just running a decimator tool on their creations and calling it a day, resulting in visibly broken Quest avatars (missing polygons, holes, bad rigging, no visemes). Seen some yesterday.\n\nI too was thinking about Quest-only worlds, actually I don’t think there’s anything wrong with these.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-05-22T15:12:51.211Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This has been my biggest frustration so far using the Quest.  Long term I imagine is to have the PC / Mobile userbase not be so divided, but in the short term it's a lackluster experience ending up in worlds filled with grey robots who don't care about using cross platform avatars.\n\nI'm considering creating a Quest-only meetup worlds as a stop-gap in the interim but am not sure if that would even get through community labs.\n\nI understand dev-created solutions to this probably aren't on the roadmap, but any suggestions on solutions on how to connect with more Quest users would be appreciated.\n\nStill really excited about the platform and am glad ya'll are working hard to continue to improve and support it.",
